<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Execute (254)</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>execute &lt;shell command&gt;
</pre>
<p>Adds a line to the file execute.dat in the lib directory, as a command 
for the server's operating system, and writes "EXECUTE(&lt;your name&gt;): 
&lt;command&gt;" to the log. You are told "Executing &lt;command&gt;." The characters 
` and&#160;; are refused, and the attempt is logged as a possible break-in.
</p><p>The game itself runs nothing: the file was meant to be run by the scripts 
that restart the game. No script in the repository reads execute.dat 
today, so unless your server has one of its own, the line is only 
stored.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Reboot</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Shutdown</a>
</pre>




</div>